      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Dalakas proposed diagnostic criteria for stiff-person syndrome",
      "quote": "Dalakas proposed diagnostic criteria for stiff-person syndrome, brieﬂy summarized as follows: (1) muscular rigidity in the limbs and axial muscles; (2) continuous cocontraction of agonist and antagonist muscles; (3) episodic spasms precipitated by unexpected noises, tactile stimuli, or emotional upset; (4) absence of any other neurologic disease that could explain stiffness and rigidity; and (5) positive antiglutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD) 65 (or amphiphysin) antibodies",
